WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.850
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Friday, November 20.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.760
Buying time!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.860
Sydney researchers report keeping a human liver alive outside the body for a record seven weeks.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.640
And a newly approved US drug helps kids wi

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.250
th a rare brain disease live years longer.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.050
Anthropic, the maker of Claude,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.460
went public in the biggest IPO ever, and vowed to pace its AI.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.430
Google's new Gemini 4 Neon, a faster mid-size model,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.890
claims top marks on tough science and maths tests.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.570
Google also built a whole fake internet to test

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.370
its web-browsing AI agents against hidden tricks.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.260
And UCSF found where the brain drafts each word b

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.550
efore we speak: a new target for speech implants.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.260
On to longevity. Sydney's Actinogen says its Alzheimer's pill missed overall,

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.380
but more over-75s held steady.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.180
In people with Down syndrome,

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.950
other genes can shift when Alzheimer's starts by about a decade.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.020
And in human spinal disc cells,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.590
boosting one little-known protein cut signs of ageing and DNA damage.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.260
And a big review found activity and fitness tr

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.080
ack with a longer life far more than diet does.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.250
On to wellbeing. In a small trial,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.530
gentle currents from scalp electrodes eased mild depression, no surgery needed.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.250
And at Yale,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.110
kids who played a Lego Batman racing game right before surgery stayed calmer.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.020
Now, the catch.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:51.680
A Lancet commission says over one in ten people may have problematic internet use.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.310
And Reuters reports Meta's AI agent Muse mixed up staff chats,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.700
surfacing other people's private data.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.640
In Brisbane,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.830
UQ physicists sent a message through a brick wall using gravity and an old lift.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.890
In Shenzhen, 151 humanoid robots danced in sync for a Guinness world record.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.120
And in early tests,

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.970
a Hong Kong smart floss tracked blood sugar using fluid from around the gums.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.910
Anthropic's boss thinks AI could fit a century of progress into a decade.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.610
Until then? Buying time.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
